cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Corless's nilpotent conjecture: proof, Lean formalisation and computations"
authors:
  - family-names: Blattner
    given-names: Marcel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-7188-673X"
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24317787
repository-code: "https://github.com/marcelbtec/corless-nilpotent"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A proof of Conjecture 5.1 of R. M. Corless (Maple Transactions, 2021): the
  recursively constructed vectors give all nilpotent skew-symmetric tridiagonal
  matrices with superdiagonal entries in {1, i}, and there are exactly 2^(K-1)
  of them in dimension 2^K - 1. The proof reduces nilpotency modulo 4 to a
  linear system over F_2. It is formalised in Lean 4 with Mathlib. Python and
  C scripts check every step numerically and extend the exhaustive
  verification from m = 31 to m = 63.
keywords:
  - Bohemian matrices
  - nilpotent matrices
  - skew-symmetric tridiagonal matrices
  - matching polynomial
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Corless
